[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:But not Murder!]
[00:13.52]Do you think that the writer passed his driving test? Why?
[00:22.83]I was being tested for a driving licence for the third time.
[00:29.21]I had been asked to drive in heavy traffic and had done so successfully.
[00:35.92]After having been instructed to drive out of town,
[00:40.27]I began to acquire confidence.
[00:43.91]Sure that I had passed, I was almost beginning to enjoy my test.
[00:51.12]The examiner must have been pleased with my performance, for he smiled and said,
[00:58.42]'Just one more thing Mr.Eames.
[01:02.06]Let us suppose that a child suddenly crosses the road in front of you.
[01:09.09]As soon as I tap on the window, you must stop within five feet.'
[01:17.83]I continued driving and after some time,
[01:22.10]the examiner tapped loudly.
[01:25.80]Though the sound could be heard clearly, it took me a long time to react.
[01:33.95]I suddenly pressed the brake pedal hard and we were both thrown forward.
[01:41.56]The examiner looked at me sadly.
[01:46.21]'Mr. Eames,' he said, in a mournful voice,'you have just killed that child!'
